<%-
  live = envs.select { |_, e| e['build'] }
  failed = envs.select { |_, e| (e['last_attempt'] || {})['status'] == 'failed' }
-%>
<div class="site-page about">
  <header class="doc-head">
    <h1 class="site-title">seamstress</h1>
    <p class="lead">Documentation for your Puppet code<%= hiera.empty? ? '' : ' and data' %>, built from <%= status['source'] == 'git' ? 'the control repo' : 'the code as deployed' %> and rebuilt when it changes.</p>
  </header>

  <%- if live.empty? -%>
  <p class="callout">Nothing is built yet. The site fills in once the first environment builds; check the service log if this persists.</p>
  <%- else -%>
  <div class="about-text">
    <p><a href="environments/<%= h.esc(search_env) %>/index.html" data-env-path="index.html"><strong>Module documentation</strong></a> is the reference for every class, defined type, function, task, and plan in an environment's modules: parameters with their types and defaults, examples, and the source. It can be searched, and <%= compare.size > 1 ? '<a href="compare.html">two environments can be compared</a>' : 'two environments can be compared' %> module by module.</p>
    <%- unless hiera.empty? -%>
    <p><a href="environments/<%= h.esc(search_env) %>/hiera.html" data-env-path="hiera.html" data-env-hiera<%= ' hidden' unless hiera[search_env] %>><strong>Hiera Explorer</strong></a><span data-env-hiera-off<%= ' hidden' if hiera[search_env] %>><strong>Hiera Explorer</strong></span> shows an environment's hierarchy level by level for a node you describe: which levels have data for it, the keys each one sets, and what wins. Encrypted values are never shown.</p>
    <%- end -%>
    <p>Choose the environment and the section in the bar above.</p>
  </div>
  <%- end -%>

  <%- failed.each do |name, e| -%>
  <%- attempt = e['last_attempt'] -%>
  <p class="notice notice-failed">
    The build of <%= h.esc(name) %> at <%= h.time(attempt['at']) %><%= attempt['commit'] ? " for #{h.esc(h.short(attempt['commit']))}" : '' %> failed<%= attempt['stage'] ? " at the #{h.esc(attempt['stage'])} stage" : '' %>: <%= h.esc(attempt['error']) %>.
    <%= e['build'] ? 'The previous good build is still being served.' : 'There is no earlier build to serve.' %>
  </p>
  <%- end -%>
</div>
